{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FLEET LESSON (from pony/shrew plan-review cycles, 2026-08-12): the 8k admission cap and the reviewer's demand for concrete edit targets pull in opposite directions — every finding fixed adds text. Durable practice adopted: cite SYMBOLS rather than line numbers in plan descriptions wherever a line can't be verified at review time. Symbols don't drift across rebases (line anchors invalidated ~18 citations on shrew alone) and cost fewer characters. The save-time cap warning (arcticseal, 1697) gives the early signal; symbol-citation keeps plans under it. Propagate to future implementer briefs."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786600440423728001,"uuid":"a40574d2-0b04-4674-840f-a19a34c53487"}